IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-solvency`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 78A, 78B and 78C -- Division 3A, reduction of share capital: the preliminary rules, and the
-- reduction by a private company and by a public company (the solvency statement, the inspection duties, the lodgement).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 9300-9500 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- Tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).
-- "beginning with" and "ending with" count the day named as day 1 (fork F-P1): the keel's `period: ...` functions are called with the count less one.

§ `Section 78A: Division 3A, preliminary`

-- (5), (5A), (6): the three cases to which "This Division does not apply". TRUE where the text says the Division does not apply; the text lists them without "only", so any other case is NOTHING.
-- src:9344 | (5) This Division does not apply to an unlimited company, and does
-- src:9345 | not preclude such a company from reducing in any way its share
-- src:9346 | capital.
-- src:9348 | (5A) This Division does not apply to any redemption of preference
-- src:9349 | shares issued by a company under section 70(1) which results in a
-- src:9350 | reduction in the company’s share capital.
-- src:9354 | (6) This Division does not apply to the purchase or acquisition or
-- src:9355 | proposed purchase or acquisition by a company of its own shares in
-- src:9356 | accordance with sections 76B to 76G.
@ref s 78A(5) (src:9344-9356)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the reduction is a redemption of preference shares issued by the company under section 70(1) which results in a reduction in the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction is the purchase or acquisition or proposed purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78A(5) this Division does not apply to the company or the reduction` MEANS
    IF    (`s 4(1) "unlimited company" the company is an unlimited company` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR `the reduction is a redemption of preference shares issued by the company under section 70(1) which results in a reduction in the company's share capital`
       OR `the reduction is the purchase or acquisition or proposed purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division does not apply to an unlimited company"; "does not apply to any redemption of preference shares issued by a company under section 70(1)"; "does not apply to the purchase or acquisition ... in accordance with sections 76B to 76G" -- three cases named, no word saying they are the only ones {F-A1} {MR-b}

-- (1): "A company may reduce its share capital under the provisions of this Division in any way". A grant: the gates are the three exclusions and the constitution's power in (3).
-- src:9304 | 78A.—(1) A company may reduce its share capital under the
-- src:9305 | provisions of this Division in any way and, in particular, do all or any
-- src:9306 | of the following:
-- src:9308 | (a) extinguish or reduce the liability on any of its shares in
-- src:9309 | respect of share capital not paid up;
-- src:9311 | (b) cancel any paid‑up share capital which is lost or
-- src:9312 | unrepresented by available assets;
-- src:9314 | (c) return to shareholders any paid‑up share capital which is
-- src:9315 | more than it needs.
@ref s 78A(1) (src:9304-9315)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the reduction is a redemption of preference shares issued by the company under section 70(1) which results in a reduction in the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction is the purchase or acquisition or proposed purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the constitution of the company excludes or restricts the power to reduce share capital which this Division confers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78A(1) the company may reduce its share capital under the provisions of this Division` MEANS
    IF    (`s 78A(5) this Division does not apply to the company or the reduction` liability `the reduction is a redemption of preference shares issued by the company under section 70(1) which results in a reduction in the company's share capital` `the reduction is the purchase or acquisition or proposed purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR `the constitution of the company excludes or restricts the power to reduce share capital which this Division confers`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company may reduce its share capital under the provisions of this Division in any way"; where the Division does not apply, or the constitution excludes or restricts the power (subsection (3) says what the constitution may do, not what follows for subsection (1)), the grant is not made and the subsection says nothing further, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 {F-A1} {F-A2} {MR-b}
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2): "A company may not reduce its share capital in any way except by a procedure provided for it by the provisions of this Division." A bar: TRUE where the reduction is barred.
-- src:9317 | (2) A company may not reduce its share capital in any way except
-- src:9318 | by a procedure provided for it by the provisions of this Division.
@ref s 78A(2) (src:9317-9318)
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the reduction is a redemption of preference shares issued by the company under section 70(1) which results in a reduction in the company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction is the purchase or acquisition or proposed purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company reduces its share capital by a procedure provided for it by the provisions of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78A(2) the reduction of share capital is barred` MEANS
    IF `s 4(1) "unlimited company" the company is an unlimited company` liability EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Division does not apply to an unlimited company, and does not preclude such a company from reducing in any way its share capital" (subsection (5), a flat negative) {F-A1} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF `the reduction is a redemption of preference shares issued by the company under section 70(1) which results in a reduction in the company's share capital` OR `the reduction is the purchase or acquisition or proposed purchase or acquisition by the company of its own shares in accordance with sections 76B to 76G`
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division does not apply to any redemption of preference shares" and "does not apply to the purchase or acquisition ... in accordance with sections 76B to 76G"; the bar is part of the Division, so it does not reach these, and what does bar them is outside this text {F-A1} {MR-b}
          ELSE (IF `the company reduces its share capital by a procedure provided for it by the provisions of this Division`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company may not reduce its share capital in any way except by a procedure provided for it by the provisions of this Division" -- the "except" is met {MR-a}
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- (3): "A company's constitution may exclude or restrict any power to reduce share capital conferred on the company by this Division."
-- src:9320 | (3) A company’s constitution may exclude or restrict any power to
-- src:9321 | reduce share capital conferred on the company by this Division.
@ref s 78A(3) (src:9320-9321)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company excludes or restricts a power to reduce share capital conferred on the company by this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78A(3) the constitution may exclude or restrict the power` MEANS
    IF `the constitution of the company excludes or restricts a power to reduce share capital conferred on the company by this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a permission to the constitution ("may exclude or restrict"); a constitution that does not do so is not mentioned, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 {MR-b}

-- (4) "reduction information": "means the following information: (a) the amount of the company's share capital that is thereby reduced; (b) the number of shares that are thereby cancelled".
-- src:9328 | (4) In this Division —
-- src:9330 | “reduction information”, in relation to a proposed reduction of
-- src:9331 | share capital by a special resolution of a company, means the
-- src:9332 | following information:
-- src:9334 | (a) the amount of the company’s share capital that is
-- src:9335 | thereby reduced;
-- src:9337 | (b) the number of shares that are thereby cancelled;
@ref s 78A(4) "reduction information" (src:9328-9337)
GIVEN `the information is about a proposed reduction of share capital by a special resolution of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the amount of the company's share capital that is thereby reduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information states the number of shares that are thereby cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78A(4) "reduction information" the information is reduction information` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information is about a proposed reduction of share capital by a special resolution of the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "“reduction information”, in relation to a proposed reduction of share capital by a special resolution of a company"; any other reduction is outside the definition {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the information states the amount of the company's share capital that is thereby reduced` AND `the information states the number of shares that are thereby cancelled`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“reduction information” ... means the following information: (a) the amount of the company’s share capital that is thereby reduced; (b) the number of shares that are thereby cancelled" (a "means" definition, read as both items required) {F-A3}

-- (4) "resolution date": "in relation to a resolution, means the date when the resolution is passed".
-- src:9339 | “resolution date”, in relation to a resolution, means the date
-- src:9340 | when the resolution is passed.
@ref s 78A(4) "resolution date" (src:9339-9340)
GIVEN `the date the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78A(4) "resolution date" the resolution date` MEANS `the date the resolution is passed`

§ `Section 78B: reduction of share capital by a private company`

-- (1): the grant. The company must be a private company limited by shares; the resolution special; the solvency requirements met (unless (2) lets the company off them) and the prescribed publicity requirements met.
-- src:9360 | 78B.—(1) A private company limited by shares may reduce its
-- src:9361 | share capital in any way by a special resolution if the company —
-- src:9363 | (a) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]
-- src:9365 | (b) meets the solvency requirements; and
-- src:9367 | (c) meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by
-- src:9368 | the Minister,
-- src:9370 | but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital take effect
-- src:9371 | only as provided by section 78E.
@ref s 78B(1) (src:9360-9371)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      liability IS A `Liability of members`
      `the reduction is made by a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets the solvency requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(1) the private company limited by shares may reduce its share capital in any way by a special resolution` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a private company`) OR ((`s 4(1) "company limited by shares" the company is a company limited by shares` liability) EQUALS JUST FALSE)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company limited by shares may reduce its share capital"; a public company, or a private company that is not limited by shares, is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the reduction is made by a special resolution`
            AND (((`s 78B(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the company meets the solvency requirements`)
            AND `the company meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by the Minister`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may reduce its share capital in any way by a special resolution if the company — ... (b) meets the solvency requirements; and (c) meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by the Minister" -- a grant named "may" whose "if" gate is not met, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 (a "where/when/upon" gate would be listed without deciding; this one is an "if") {F-A4} {MR-b}

-- (2): "Despite subsection (1), the company need not meet the solvency requirements if the reduction of share capital does not involve any of the following: (a) a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company; (b) a release of any liability owed to the company."
-- src:9375 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the company need not meet the solvency
-- src:9376 | requirements if the reduction of share capital does not involve any of
-- src:9377 | the following:
-- src:9382 | (a) a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the
-- src:9383 | company;
-- src:9385 | (b) a release of any liability owed to the company.
@ref s 78B(2) (src:9375-9385)
GIVEN `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company`) AND (NOT `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company need not meet the solvency requirements if the reduction of share capital does not involve any of the following" -- a dispensation, no "only if"; where the reduction involves one of them, subsection (1) still asks for the solvency requirements and this subsection is silent {F-A4} {MR-b}

-- (3): "the company meets the solvency requirements if — (a) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement in relation to the reduction of capital; and (b) the statement is made — (i) in time for subsection (4)(a) to be complied with; but (ii) not before the beginning of the period of 20 days ending with the resolution date."
-- The period of 20 days ending with the resolution date begins 19 days before it (fork F-P1).
-- src:9389 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), the company meets the
-- src:9390 | solvency requirements if —
-- src:9392 | (a) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement
-- src:9393 | in relation to the reduction of capital; and
-- src:9395 | (b) the statement is made —
-- src:9397 | (i) in time for subsection (4)(a) to be complied with; but
-- src:9399 | (ii) not before the beginning of the period of 20 days
-- src:9400 | ending with the resolution date.
@ref s 78B(3) (src:9389-9400)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors of the company make the solvency statement in relation to the reduction of capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the last day by which subsection (4)(a) must be complied with` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(3) the company meets the solvency requirements` MEANS
    IF    `all the directors of the company make the solvency statement in relation to the reduction of capital`
      AND ((`s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` statement `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND (statement's `the proposal it concerns` EQUALS `a reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C`)
      AND (statement's `the date of the statement` AT MOST `the last day by which subsection (4)(a) must be complied with`)
      AND (statement's `the date of the statement` AT LEAST `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the resolution date` 19 Days)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; the subsection's "if" is unmet): "the company meets the solvency requirements if — (a) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement in relation to the reduction of capital; and (b) the statement is made — (i) in time for subsection (4)(a) to be complied with; but (ii) not before the beginning of the period of 20 days ending with the resolution date" {F-A5} {F-A6} {MR-a}

-- (4) the lead-in "Unless subsection (2) applies": a flat negative when it applies (no duty, so no contravention).
-- (4)(a): "(i) if the resolution ... is a special resolution to be passed by written means under section 184A — ensure that every copy of the resolution served under section 183(3A) or 184C(1) (as the case may be) is accompanied by a copy of the solvency statement; or (ii) if the resolution is a special resolution to be passed in a general meeting — throughout that meeting make the solvency statement or a copy of it available for inspection by the members at that meeting".
DECLARE `s 78B(4)(a) how the special resolution is to be passed` IS ONE OF
    `s 78B(4)(a)(i) by written means under section 184A`
    `s 78B(4)(a)(ii) in a general meeting`
    `s 78B(4)(a) in some other way`

-- src:9404 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company —
-- src:9406 | (a) must —
-- src:9408 | (i) if the resolution for reducing share capital is a special
-- src:9409 | resolution to be passed by written means under
-- src:9410 | section 184A — ensure that every copy of the
-- src:9411 | resolution served under section 183(3A) or 184C(1)
-- src:9412 | (as the case may be) is accompanied by a copy of the
-- src:9413 | solvency statement; or
-- src:9415 | (ii) if the resolution is a special resolution to be passed in
-- src:9416 | a general meeting — throughout that meeting make
-- src:9417 | the solvency statement or a copy of it available for
-- src:9418 | inspection by the members at that meeting; and
@ref s 78B(4)(a) (src:9404-9418)
GIVEN way IS A `s 78B(4)(a) how the special resolution is to be passed`
      `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every copy of the resolution served under section 183(3A) or 184C(1) is accompanied by a copy of the solvency statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the solvency statement or a copy of it was available for inspection by the members throughout the general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(4)(a) the company has contravened paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF (`s 78B(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless subsection (2) applies, the company — (a) must —" -- subsection (2) applies, so the duty does not arise (a duty not engaged, the provision's own question) {F-A5} {MR-a}
    ELSE (CONSIDER way
          WHEN `s 78B(4)(a)(i) by written means under section 184A` THEN JUST (NOT `every copy of the resolution served under section 183(3A) or 184C(1) is accompanied by a copy of the solvency statement`)
          WHEN `s 78B(4)(a)(ii) in a general meeting` THEN JUST (NOT `the solvency statement or a copy of it was available for inspection by the members throughout the general meeting`)
          OTHERWISE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (a) names a special resolution passed by written means under section 184A and one passed in a general meeting; a resolution passed some other way is outside it {MR-b}

-- (4)(b): "must, throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at the company's registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor of the company."
-- The 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date end on the 41st day after it (fork F-P1). (6): the requirement ceases if the resolution is revoked; read as running to the day before the revocation (fork F-A7).
-- src:9432 | (6) Any requirement under subsection (4)(b) ceases if the resolution
-- src:9433 | is revoked.
@ref s 78B(6) (src:9432-9433)
GIVEN `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the resolution is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the resolution is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78B(6) the last day to which the requirement under subsection (4)(b) runs` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is revoked` AND (`the date the resolution is revoked` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 41 Days)
    THEN `the date the resolution is revoked` MINUS 1
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 41 Days

-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9404 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company —
-- src:9420 | (b) must, throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution
-- src:9421 | date, make the solvency statement or a copy of it available
-- src:9422 | at the company’s registered office for inspection free of
-- src:9423 | charge by any creditor of the company.
@ref s 78B(4)(b) (src:9404-9423)
GIVEN `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the resolution is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the resolution is revoked` IS A DATE
      `the solvency statement or a copy of it was made available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day it was so available` IS A DATE
      `the last day it was so available` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(4)(b) the company has contravened paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF (`s 78B(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless subsection (2) applies, the company — ... (b) must" -- subsection (2) applies, so the duty does not arise {F-A5} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the solvency statement or a copy of it was made available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
             AND (`the first day it was so available` AT MOST `the resolution date`)
             AND (`the last day it was so available` AT LEAST `s 78B(6) the last day to which the requirement under subsection (4)(b) runs` `the resolution date` `the resolution is revoked` `the date the resolution is revoked`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "must, throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date, make the solvency statement or a copy of it available ... for inspection free of charge by any creditor" -- the duty is met, so no contravention {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (5): "The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a contravention of subsection (4), but every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence."
-- src:9425 | (5) The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a
-- src:9426 | contravention of subsection (4), but every officer of the company who
-- src:9427 | is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78B(5) (src:9425-9427)
GIVEN `the only defect in the resolution is a contravention of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(5) the resolution is invalid by virtue only of a contravention of subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the only defect in the resolution is a contravention of subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a contravention of subsection (4)" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says a contravention of (4) alone does not invalidate the resolution; whether any other defect does is outside it

-- src:9425 | (5) The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a
-- src:9426 | contravention of subsection (4), but every officer of the company who
-- src:9427 | is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78B(5) (src:9425-9427)
GIVEN `the company has contravened subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78B(5) the officer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company has contravened subsection (4)` AND `the person is an officer of the company` AND `the officer is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i) of the brief, fork line F-A8): "every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence {F-A8} {MR-a}

-- The regulative rules. The company is the bearer of (4); no penalty is stated in these sections (the offence in (5) names none), so none is encoded (fork F-A8).
DECLARE `s 78B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78B(4)(a)(i) ensure that every copy of the resolution served is accompanied by a copy of the solvency statement`
    `s 78B(4)(a)(ii) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available for inspection by the members throughout the general meeting`
    `s 78B(4)(b) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
    `s 78B(4)(b) withdraw the solvency statement or a copy of it from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks`

-- (4)(a) names no day by which the company must act, so the rule has no deadline and cannot reach BREACH (listed in NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:9404 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company —
-- src:9406 | (a) must —
-- src:9408 | (i) if the resolution for reducing share capital is a special
-- src:9409 | resolution to be passed by written means under
-- src:9410 | section 184A — ensure that every copy of the
-- src:9411 | resolution served under section 183(3A) or 184C(1)
-- src:9412 | (as the case may be) is accompanied by a copy of the
-- src:9413 | solvency statement; or
-- src:9415 | (ii) if the resolution is a special resolution to be passed in
-- src:9416 | a general meeting — throughout that meeting make
-- src:9417 | the solvency statement or a copy of it available for
-- src:9418 | inspection by the members at that meeting; and
@ref s 78B(4)(a) (src:9404-9418)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      way IS A `s 78B(4)(a) how the special resolution is to be passed`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78B act`
`s 78B(4)(a) the company must make the solvency statement available as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 78B(4)(a)(i) by written means under section 184A` THEN PARTY Company `the name of the company` MUST `s 78B(4)(a)(i) ensure that every copy of the resolution served is accompanied by a copy of the solvency statement` HENCE FULFILLED
    WHEN `s 78B(4)(a)(ii) in a general meeting` THEN PARTY Company `the name of the company` MUST `s 78B(4)(a)(ii) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available for inspection by the members throughout the general meeting` HENCE FULFILLED
    OTHERWISE FULFILLED

-- (4)(b): "throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date" cannot be written as one "within": the statement must be there from day 0 (the resolution date), and must not be taken away up to day 41. Day 0 is the resolution date (fork F-A10).
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9404 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company —
-- src:9420 | (b) must, throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution
-- src:9421 | date, make the solvency statement or a copy of it available
-- src:9422 | at the company’s registered office for inspection free of
-- src:9423 | charge by any creditor of the company.
@ref s 78B(4)(b) (src:9404-9423)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78B act`
`s 78B(4)(b) the company must make the solvency statement available throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 78B(4)(b) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
           SHANT `s 78B(4)(b) withdraw the solvency statement or a copy of it from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks`
           WITHIN 41
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at its registered office for inspection by creditors from the resolution date"

§ `Section 78C: reduction of share capital by a public company`

-- (1): the same grant for a public company.
-- src:9437 | 78C.—(1) A public company may reduce its share capital in any
-- src:9438 | way by a special resolution if the company —
-- src:9440 | (a) [Deleted by Act 36 of 2014]
-- src:9442 | (b) meets the solvency requirements; and
-- src:9444 | (c) meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by
-- src:9445 | the Minister,
-- src:9447 | but the resolution and the reduction of the share capital take effect
-- src:9448 | only as provided by section 78E.
@ref s 78C(1) (src:9437-9448)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction is made by a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets the solvency requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(1) the public company may reduce its share capital in any way by a special resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company may reduce its share capital"; a private company is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the reduction is made by a special resolution`
            AND (((`s 78C(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the company meets the solvency requirements`)
            AND `the company meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by the Minister`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may reduce its share capital in any way by a special resolution if the company — ... (b) meets the solvency requirements; and (c) meets such publicity requirements as may be prescribed by the Minister" -- a grant named "may" whose "if" gate is not met, the grant rule of 2026-11-12 limit 1 {F-A4} {MR-b}

-- src:9450 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the company need not meet the solvency
-- src:9451 | requirements if the reduction of share capital does not involve any of
-- src:9452 | the following:
-- src:9454 | (a) a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the
-- src:9455 | company;
-- src:9457 | (b) a release of any liability owed to the company.
@ref s 78C(2) (src:9450-9457)
GIVEN `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company`) AND (NOT `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company need not meet the solvency requirements if the reduction of share capital does not involve any of the following" -- a dispensation, no "only if" {F-A4} {MR-b}

-- (3): the same two limbs with 30 days (the period of 30 days ending with the resolution date begins 29 days before it), and (c): the copy of the statement is lodged with the copy of the resolution required by section 186, within the 15 days beginning with the resolution date.
-- (6): "Any requirement under subsection (3)(c) or (4)(b) ceases if the resolution is revoked." Read as: a resolution revoked on or before the last day for lodging needs no lodgement (fork F-A11).
-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9461 | (3) The company meets the solvency requirements if —
-- src:9463 | (a) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement
-- src:9464 | in relation to the reduction of share capital;
-- src:9466 | (b) the statement is made —
-- src:9468 | (i) in time for subsection (4)(a) to be complied with; but
-- src:9470 | (ii) not before the beginning of the period of 30 days
-- src:9471 | ending with the resolution date; and
-- src:9473 | (c) a copy of the solvency statement is lodged with the
-- src:9474 | Registrar, together with the copy of the resolution required
-- src:9475 | to be lodged with the Registrar under section 186, within
-- src:9476 | 15 days beginning with the resolution date.
@ref s 78C(3) (src:9461-9476)
GIVEN statement IS A `Solvency statement`
      `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the directors of the company make the solvency statement in relation to the reduction of share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the last day by which subsection (4)(a) must be complied with` IS A DATE
      `a copy of the solvency statement is lodged with the Registrar, together with the copy of the resolution required to be lodged with the Registrar under section 186` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the copy of the solvency statement is lodged` IS A DATE
      `the resolution is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the resolution is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(3) the company meets the solvency requirements` MEANS
    IF    `all the directors of the company make the solvency statement in relation to the reduction of share capital`
      AND ((`s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` statement `the company is exempt from audit requirements under section 205B or 205C`) EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND (statement's `the proposal it concerns` EQUALS `a reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C`)
      AND (statement's `the date of the statement` AT MOST `the last day by which subsection (4)(a) must be complied with`)
      AND (statement's `the date of the statement` AT LEAST `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the resolution date` 29 Days)
      AND (   (`a copy of the solvency statement is lodged with the Registrar, together with the copy of the resolution required to be lodged with the Registrar under section 186`
               AND (`the date the copy of the solvency statement is lodged` AT LEAST `the resolution date`) AND (`the date the copy of the solvency statement is lodged` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 14 Days))
           OR (`the resolution is revoked` AND (`the date the resolution is revoked` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 14 Days)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; the subsection's "if" is unmet): "The company meets the solvency requirements if — (a) all the directors of the company make a solvency statement ...; (b) the statement is made — (i) in time for subsection (4)(a) to be complied with; but (ii) not before the beginning of the period of 30 days ending with the resolution date; and (c) a copy of the solvency statement is lodged with the Registrar ... within 15 days beginning with the resolution date" {F-A5} {F-A6} {F-A11} {MR-a}

-- src:9483 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company must —
-- src:9485 | (a) throughout the meeting at which the resolution is to be
-- src:9486 | passed — make the solvency statement or a copy of it
-- src:9487 | available for inspection by the members at the meeting;
@ref s 78C(4)(a) (src:9483-9487)
GIVEN `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the solvency statement or a copy of it was available for inspection by the members throughout the meeting at which the resolution was to be passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(4)(a) the company has contravened paragraph (a)` MEANS
    IF (`s 78C(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless subsection (2) applies, the company must —" -- subsection (2) applies, so the duty does not arise {F-A5} {MR-a}
    ELSE JUST (NOT `the solvency statement or a copy of it was available for inspection by the members throughout the meeting at which the resolution was to be passed`)

-- src:9499 | (6) Any requirement under subsection (3)(c) or (4)(b) ceases if the
-- src:9500 | resolution is revoked.
@ref s 78C(6) (src:9499-9500)
GIVEN `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the resolution is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the resolution is revoked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78C(6) the last day to which the requirement under subsection (4)(b) runs` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is revoked` AND (`the date the resolution is revoked` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 41 Days)
    THEN `the date the resolution is revoked` MINUS 1
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the resolution date` 41 Days

-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9483 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company must —
-- src:9490 | (b) throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution
-- src:9491 | date — make the solvency statement or a copy of it
-- src:9492 | available at the company’s registered office for inspection
-- src:9493 | free of charge by any creditor of the company.
@ref s 78C(4)(b) (src:9483-9493)
GIVEN `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution date` IS A DATE
      `the resolution is revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the resolution is revoked` IS A DATE
      `the solvency statement or a copy of it was made available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first day it was so available` IS A DATE
      `the last day it was so available` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(4)(b) the company has contravened paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF (`s 78C(2) the company need not meet the solvency requirements` `the reduction involves a reduction or distribution of cash or other assets by the company` `the reduction involves a release of any liability owed to the company`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless subsection (2) applies, the company must — ... (b) throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date" -- subsection (2) applies, so the duty does not arise {F-A5} {MR-a}
    ELSE (IF    `the solvency statement or a copy of it was made available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
             AND (`the first day it was so available` AT MOST `the resolution date`)
             AND (`the last day it was so available` AT LEAST `s 78C(6) the last day to which the requirement under subsection (4)(b) runs` `the resolution date` `the resolution is revoked` `the date the resolution is revoked`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date — make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at the company's registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor" -- the duty is met, so no contravention {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:9495 | (5) The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a
-- src:9496 | contravention of subsection (4), but every officer of the company who
-- src:9497 | is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78C(5) (src:9495-9497)
GIVEN `the only defect in the resolution is a contravention of subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(5) the resolution is invalid by virtue only of a contravention of subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the only defect in the resolution is a contravention of subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a contravention of subsection (4)" (a flat negative) {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says a contravention of (4) alone does not invalidate the resolution; whether any other defect does is outside it

-- src:9495 | (5) The resolution does not become invalid by virtue only of a
-- src:9496 | contravention of subsection (4), but every officer of the company who
-- src:9497 | is in default shall be guilty of an offence.
@ref s 78C(5) (src:9495-9497)
GIVEN `the company has contravened subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78C(5) the officer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company has contravened subsection (4)` AND `the person is an officer of the company` AND `the officer is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i) of the brief, fork line F-A8): "every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts {F-A8} {MR-a}

DECLARE `s 78C act` IS ONE OF
    `s 78C(4)(a) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available for inspection by the members throughout the meeting at which the resolution is to be passed`
    `s 78C(4)(b) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
    `s 78C(4)(b) withdraw the solvency statement or a copy of it from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks`

-- (4)(a) names no day by which the company must act: no deadline, no breach path (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path").
-- src:9483 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company must —
-- src:9485 | (a) throughout the meeting at which the resolution is to be
-- src:9486 | passed — make the solvency statement or a copy of it
-- src:9487 | available for inspection by the members at the meeting;
@ref s 78C(4)(a) (src:9483-9487)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78C act`
`s 78C(4)(a) the company must make the solvency statement available throughout the meeting` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 78C(4)(a) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available for inspection by the members throughout the meeting at which the resolution is to be passed`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- This period is counted with the day named as day 1, so the keel is called with the count less one (fork F-P1).
-- src:9483 | (4) Unless subsection (2) applies, the company must —
-- src:9490 | (b) throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution
-- src:9491 | date — make the solvency statement or a copy of it
-- src:9492 | available at the company’s registered office for inspection
-- src:9493 | free of charge by any creditor of the company.
@ref s 78C(4)(b) (src:9483-9493)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 78C act`
`s 78C(4)(b) the company must make the solvency statement available throughout the 6 weeks beginning with the resolution date` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 78C(4)(b) make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at the registered office for inspection free of charge by any creditor`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
           SHANT `s 78C(4)(b) withdraw the solvency statement or a copy of it from inspection by creditors before the end of the 6 weeks`
           WITHIN 41
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not make the solvency statement or a copy of it available at its registered office for inspection by creditors from the resolution date"
